# scripts/leak-check.exclude
#
# Glob list of relative paths (relative to the scanned root) that the
# leak check must skip. One glob per line; comments and blank lines are
# ignored.
#
# Keep this minimal. Prefer writing self-clean patterns (see the note in
# scripts/leak-check.patterns) and cleaning the offending value, and only
# exclude a path when it genuinely cannot be made clean — with a comment
# below saying why.

# (none)

# Generated kernel BTF headers (btfgen output): the 16-bit device/vendor
# constants inside them belong to the kernel image, not to this machine,
# and the header must be regenerated, not hand-edited. These paths
# genuinely cannot be made clean, so they are excluded.
internal/observer/ebpf/vmlinux_amd64/vmlinux.h
internal/observer/ebpf/vmlinux_arm64/vmlinux.h

# The allowed-address list names the public cloud metadata constants it allows.
scripts/leak-check.allowed-addresses
